        <briefdescription>
<para>Compute the Mahalanobis distance analysis of residuals with respect to the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref>. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The squared Mahalanobis distance is d² = rᵀ P⁻¹ r, where r are the residuals and P the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref> coordinates. The p-value is the survival function of the chi-squared distribution with as many degrees of freedom as the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref> size, evaluated at d².</para>
<para><ulink url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahalanobis_distance">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahalanobis_distance</ulink></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>aResiduals</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The residuals, expressed in the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref> frame and ordered as its coordinate subsets </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>The Mahalanobis distance analysis </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ostk::core::error::runtime::Wrong</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>If the residuals size does not match the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref> size, or if the <ref refid="classostk_1_1astrodynamics_1_1uncertainty_1_1_covariance" kindref="compound">Covariance</ref> is empty or not positive definite </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
